	extsc{OSS-Instruct} generates problems from open-source code using a teacher model. Therefore, the theoretical maximum accuracy of the 	extsc{OSS-Instruct} dataset should closely match the teacher model's accuracy in analyzing and interpreting open-source code 	extit{c}. Thus, we get $\mathcal{A}_{OSS} \approx \mathcal{P}(	extit{p} \mid 	extit{c})$. 
For 	extsc{AIEV-Instruct}, we align problem descriptions and code by asking LLMs to add unit tests to the original code. After adding unit tests, we can obtain new code $	extit{c}^*$ and new problem descriptions $	extit{p}^*$. Here, we can make an assumption: $\mathcal{P}(	extit{p} \mid 	extit{c}) < \mathcal{P}(	extit{p}^* \mid 	extit{c}^*)$. This is because LLMs usually find it easier to align problem descriptions with unit tests. For example, suppose we need to write a program 	exttt{is\_prime} to detect prime numbers in a list. It is easy to validate the code by providing a few unit tests such as 	exttt{assert is\_prime([2,3,4]) == [2,3]} but ensuring that the corresponding program is entirely correct is not as straightforward. with iterative validation and correction, the probability of correctness improves with each iteration. If the probability of error in each iteration is $1 - \mathcal{P}(	extit{p}^* \mid 	extit{c}^*)$, and assuming each iteration is independent, the probability of correctness after $n$ iterations is: $\mathcal{A}_{AIEV} \approx 1 - (1 - \mathcal{P}(	extit{p}^* \mid 	extit{c}^*))^n > 1 - (1 - \mathcal{P}(	extit{p} \mid 	extit{c}))^n$. 

While prior probability of problems $\mathcal{P}(	extit{p})$ is greater than the prior probability of code $\mathcal{P}(	extit{c})$ and the iteration times $n$ is greater than $1$. We can get: 
\[
\mathcal{A}_{Evol} \approx \mathcal{P}(	extit{c} \mid 	extit{p}) =  rac{\mathcal{P}(	extit{p} \mid 	extit{c})  \cdot \mathcal{P}(	extit{c})}{\mathcal{P}(	extit{p})}
< \mathcal{P}(	extit{p} \mid 	extit{c}) \approx \mathcal{A}_{OSS} < 1 - (1 - \mathcal{P}(	extit{p} \mid 	extit{c}))^n < \mathcal{A}_{AIEV}\]
Thus, under these assumptions, the accuracy of 	extit{AutoCoder-AIEV-Instruct} should be higher than that of 	extit{Magicoder-OSS-Instruct} and 	extit{Magicoder-Evol-Instruct}.

